Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-28-2000||12:57 AM||||Hey,<BR>I finally got pictures of my 84 Hybrid.  The interior is my favorite part.  Oh yeah, there are some pictures of my Fiero sitting next to my Delorean, for those who were asking.  Check all of the pictures out here: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/myride.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/myride.html</A> <P>Here are a couple of pics.  Tell me what you think,<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/thumb2a.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/int2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||09-28-2000||03:28 AM||||Oh man, that's a nice interior, alright.  But your page mentions "all-time driving lights".  Doesn't that just mean the headlights are stuck in the UP position?  Sounds like one of those embellished ads.  Seriously, though, I like it.  I do like the Delorean too.  Never seen a red one before.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattsfiero||09-28-2000||07:43 AM||||AWSOME!!!! I love it. Great Mod man<P>Matt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-28-2000||06:31 PM||||Mike,<P>The interior is sweet!<P>I like the aircraft gas filler door, is that something you made?  I've been meaning to machine some aluminum or stainless and make one for mine for the past year, but haven't got to it.  Please email me if you know of someone who's making them.<P>Your Delorean is very nice too!!!  Do you happen to know anyone that has one for sale?<P><BR>Cheever2,<P>I've seen them painted black (they look mean with smoked headlight covers), red, forest green, and one yellow I think.  I've even seen one painted up in red white & blue with the Domino's logo painted across it.  Talk about a Domino's Delivery Delorean! guess who owned it? wasn't me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  There are 4 that were gold plated!  Anyway, I'll admit it, I'm a Delorean nut too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||MikeSchaefer||09-28-2000||06:38 PM||||Hi,<BR>No the all-time driving lights aren't my headlights  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> although now that you mention it, I guess they could be.  The lights that look like fog lights are actually driving lights that are on whenever the car is.  I fixed the headlights last weekend, but when the pictures were took, they were stuck in the all-time driving lights position.<BR>Huggr,<BR>Yeah I know a guy with a really nice delorean for sale!  If you are seriously interested I'll get his phone #.  The price is $18,000 but the car has been perfectly restored, it is the same guy who I bought the Fiero pictured above from.  He did the gas-cap mod, it is from a harley, and it looks to be nicely fiberglassed in there.  Underneath is a fast-fill nozzle too.  I have a pair of black-outs in my garage, I just have to put them on the D, they do make them look a lot more modern, getting rid of the totally 80's headlights (which I like, but...).<BR>Thanks Matt<BR>Gotta Run, if you have any other ?s just ask.<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
